Owner bug report — RECURRENCE (chat, 2026-11-21, relayed via concept agent —
Concept.md §24 item 12 amendment, recurrence note):

The creation dialog STILL does not autoscroll to the last message, despite
task 107 having landed merged + CI green (commit d37c688; the v3.11 sweep
also landed).

KEY DIAGNOSIS REQUIREMENT: the unit tests pass while the real app
misbehaves — the test contract does not reproduce the actual runtime
geometry. jsdom-only scrollTop assertions are NOT acceptable as the
contract.

Candidates that pass fake-DOM tests but fail in a browser:
- the scroll fires before fonts/images/layout settle (then content shifts
  back);
- scrollTo called on the wrong element at runtime (e.g. a wrapper, not the
  actual overflow container);
- the {#key} step remounts reset scrollTop AFTER the scroll effect runs
  (order-of-effects problem);
- smooth scrolling canceled by concurrent layout changes;
- the full-height (§25) restructure changing which element overflows;
- sticky/fixed composer overlaying content without corresponding padding.

Fix structurally (e.g. anchor the scroll container as the single overflow
element, run scroll after two rAFs / after layout settles, re-assert on
each message append, IntersectionObserver or scroll-height watcher if
needed).

Test contract: at minimum assert against the actual built component
behavior in a LAYOUT-CAPABLE environment (e.g. happy-dom with measured
layout, or a real-browser check via the existing e2e/playwright setup if
present in the repo toolchain — process note: none was found in the repo,
so no new test-runner dependency is authorized; design the strongest
layout-capable contract available without new deps).

Scope: creation chat ONLY; /chats untouched; no new deps unless a
headless-browser test runner already exists in the repo toolchain.
